WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.370
Okay,

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.370
everyone who wants

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.370
to help me DESTROY

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.370
my enemies--

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.260
raise your hand!

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.230
Great!

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.740
we'll conquer the world…

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.809
right after I rant

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:13.849
about CHAPPiE

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:16.090
and the taxonomy of movie robots--

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.810
--on this week's episode of Angry Nerd!

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.430
First, your coments.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.939
AdRock1 responded to my

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:25.790
Top 10 Movies of 2014 list with this:

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.790
“But wait…”

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:27.790
“Michael Bay released”

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.040
“a new transformers movie…”

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.290
“Shouldn't it be on here?”

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.290
Ad Rock,

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.290
I'm worried about you.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.290
Are you on some

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.290
illicit substance?

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.290
Do you need me

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.290
to talk you down,

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.290
or call poison control?

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.290
The new robot movie CHAPPiE

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.800
makes me furious!

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.170
The odd capitalization scheme

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.390
of the title, that is.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.390
It looks like the name

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.640
of a Valley startup!

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.640
But everything else

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.489
about Neil Blomkamp's new flick

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:52.789
looks totally BLEEPING boss.

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:53.789
CHAPPiE stars

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:54.789
a computer-generated droid

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:55.789
and the trailer

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:56.789
proves how much better

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:57.789
this CG design

00:00:57.789 --> 00:00:58.789
is implemented

00:00:58.789 --> 00:00:59.920
than in Will Smith's I Robot

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:00.920
UGH!

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.329
they forgot Asimov's Eighth Law:

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.479
“Movie Robots should”

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:08.550
“NOT ape the aesthetic”
“of first-gen iMacs!”

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.550
I also like that

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.320
CHAPPiE's hero does battle

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.830
with the tiresome roles

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.330
that robots have generally been

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.610
relegated to by Hollywood.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:16.610
You see,

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.780
there are three species of movie robots.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.320
You have the cutesy servant droids

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.550
who perform repairs

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.080
and dispense comic relief.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.080
Then you have

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.080
the menacing heavies,

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.180
bad guys designed

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.220
to inflict pain.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.470
And yes, Mechagodzilla counts as a robot!

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:31.470
And finally,

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.470
you have the robot

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:33.760
as childlike naïf---

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.360
steel Pinocchios who
gradually learn about the wonders

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.700
and horrors of the world.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.700
Hollywood movies

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.700
are dominated

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.880
by the first two types,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.880
but the last one

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.230
is clearly best.

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.230
These characters are

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.060
much more involving and relatable,

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.180
and movies can use
the unique perspective of these bots

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.180
to reflect on

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.630
what it means to be human.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.630
“What’s that?

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.630
Chappie’s book?”

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.630
“Yeah!

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:56.630
It’s yours””

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:57.630
“Chappie’s got stories?”

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.630
“Chappie’s got a book!”

00:01:58.630 --> 00:01:59.630
We need more movies

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:00.630
that cast robots

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.800
as the wide-eyed outsider.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.800
But the only way

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:03.800
we'll get those

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.840
is if robot actors

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.840
refuse to take

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.340
the overfamiliar stereotyped roles.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.369
I'M TALKING TO YOU,

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:10.770
JEFF 1000!

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.879
WHAT?

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:13.800
A WIRED PROPERTY?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.330
I DON'T CARE IF IT'S

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.330
A WIRED SHOW,

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.330
THAT DROID

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:18.330
IS A TEN TON

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.330
SELL-OUT!

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:20.330
HOW DO YOU

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.330
SLEEP AT NIGHT,

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.330
JEFF 1000?

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.330
Or..

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.330
how would you sleep,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
if you were

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.330
a biological entity

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.540
that required sleep?

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.300
HEY, ARE YOU RUNNING

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.230
AN ANNOTATION TO JEFF 1000

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.230
OVER ME RIGHT NOW?

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:34.230
KNOCK IT OFF!

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.230
I'M NOT GOING

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.230
TO CROSS-PROMOTE

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:37.230
FOR THAT BLEEP.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.230
Hmmm,

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.230
I’ve gotta say

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.230
that I'm a little worried

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.230
about the fact that

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:42.230
the robot in CHAPPiE

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.230
apparently learns how to be human

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.230
from the goony bird members

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.230
of the rap group

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.230
Die Antwoord.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.769
I question their credentials!

00:02:47.769 --> 00:02:49.319
What, is there a backroom deal

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:50.450
between Blomkamp and

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.030
the Capetown Chamber of Commerce

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.030
to promote fellow

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.099
South African artists?

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:57.819
Yeah, seriously,

00:02:57.819 --> 00:02:58.819
learning how

00:02:58.819 --> 00:02:59.819
to be human

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:00.819
from Ninja and Yolandi

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:01.819
is like learning to write

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:02.819
a satisying third act

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:06.730
from M. Night Shyamalan!

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:07.730
What's your

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:08.730
favorite movie robot?

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:09.730
Let me know

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.730
in the comments,

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.730
and subscribe to the WIRED channel!

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.359
And watch my other videos over there.

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:15.359
Robot henchman,

00:03:15.359 --> 00:03:16.359
can you point

00:03:16.359 --> 00:03:17.359
at my other videos?

00:03:17.359 --> 00:03:18.359
C’mon…

00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:19.390
C’mon…

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.670
There!

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.930
I knew that you could!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:23.930
Now--

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.650
dance the Cabbage Patch for me.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:30.670
That’s not the Cabbage patch!

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.510
Go over here!

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.819
Attack that comic book!

00:03:37.819 --> 00:03:40.209
Point..

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:42.599
Point…

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:44.989
Point…

00:03:44.989 --> 00:03:47.060
I knew that you could.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.849
“Uh huh.”

00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:56.650
Easy for you to say.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:57.980
Can we get some tape for him?

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.980
He’s just…

00:03:58.980 --> 00:03:59.999
He’s not hitting his marks.

